# NanoClaw container setup. The default profile includes Mnemon's persistent
# graph memory; set NANOCLAW_SETUP=plain for a plain NanoClaw agent image.
# Both profiles are containerized only. The Anthropic API key is registered
# interactively by nanoclaw.sh on first install.

# Setup profile: mnemon (default) | plain. Switching an existing install
# requires a CLEAN deploy so the agent image is rebuilt from fresh upstream
# NanoClaw source without the previous profile's patches.
NANOCLAW_SETUP=mnemon

# The orchestrator container's name.
CONTAINER_NAME=nanoclaw-mnemon

# Absolute path where the NanoClaw repo will be cloned and installed.
# Format: An absolute path where the current user has write access, or a
# leading ~ (expanded to your home directory when this is written to .env
# via deploy.sh's TUI — plain "~"/"~/..." only, not "~otheruser/..."). This
# is bind-mounted into the orchestrator container at the SAME absolute path
# (not remapped to something else) — required so the orchestrator can
# correctly spawn per-conversation-group agent containers via the host's
# Docker socket. See the README's "Deployment Modes" section before
# changing how this is mounted.
NANOCLAW_INSTALL_PATH=~/nanoclaw-mnemon

# NanoClaw has no web UI by default (its own README: "no monitoring
# dashboard or debugging UI — describe the problem in chat"). This just
# pre-reserves a port on the container in case you later add its optional
# /add-dashboard skill (a separate npm package with its own DASHBOARD_PORT/
# DASHBOARD_SECRET, not read from this variable at all).
# Format: A valid local TCP port number.
NANOCLAW_PORT=3081

# The mnemon release version to install into NanoClaw's agent sandbox image
# — see https://github.com/mnemon-dev/mnemon/releases. Pinned rather than
# "latest" so a CLEAN redeploy doesn't silently pick up a new mnemon release
# without you choosing to.
# Format: A mnemon release tag without the leading "v" (e.g. 0.1.17).
MNEMON_VERSION=0.1.17

# Optional — enables mnemon's own built-in hybrid graph+vector recall
# (mnemon's own MNEMON_EMBED_ENDPOINT, not something this environment
# invented). Left unset, mnemon runs graph-only, which is its own
# documented default — not a degraded mode. Uncomment to enable; on
# Docker Desktop, host.docker.internal reaches whatever Ollama you have
# running on the host itself. If set, run.sh's ensure_ollama_ready()
# checks whether that endpoint is reachable and — only for a local
# address (host.docker.internal/localhost/127.0.0.1) — offers to install
# Ollama via Homebrew (macOS) or the official installer (Linux), starts
# it if it's installed but not running, and pulls the model if missing.
# Installation always asks for confirmation first; every failure here is
# a warning, never a hard stop — the rest of the deploy proceeds either
# way, with mnemon just running graph-only until this resolves.
# Requires a CLEAN redeploy to take effect on an already-deployed install
# (same as bumping MNEMON_VERSION above — the patch only applies to a
# fresh clone).
# Format: A URL mnemon's container can reach.
MNEMON_EMBED_ENDPOINT=http://host.docker.internal:11434

# Optional — overrides mnemon's own default embedding model. Leave this
# commented out to use that default (nomic-embed-text) — mnemon already
# uses it automatically once MNEMON_EMBED_ENDPOINT above is set; nothing
# here is required to get it. Only uncomment if you want a DIFFERENT
# model instead (example below is illustrative, not a recommendation).
# Only read if MNEMON_EMBED_ENDPOINT above is set.
#
# The two reasons to actually override the default:
#   - Multilingual support (nomic-embed-text itself is English-only):
#     nomic-embed-text-v2-moe (same family as the default, MoE-based),
#     bge-m3 (BAAI, also does hybrid sparse+dense retrieval), or
#     snowflake-arctic-embed2 (adds multilingual over the English-only v1).
#   - Lighter weight for constrained hardware: all-minilm (smallest/fastest,
#     lower quality) or snowflake-arctic-embed's own small tags (22m/33m).
# Whatever you pick must be pulled on the Ollama daemon first — this
# environment's ensure_ollama_ready() only auto-pulls whichever single
# model this variable resolves to, not alternatives.
#
# Format: An Ollama model name already pulled on that endpoint's daemon.
MNEMON_EMBED_MODEL=nomic-embed-text

# Optional — which model `claude` launches with inside this container's own
# admin session ("Open a Claude Session" in the deploy.sh menu — see
# scripts/claude-tmux.sh), passed as `claude --model <this>`. Does NOT
# affect per-conversation-group agent containers — those are NanoClaw's own
# separate concern (see the README's "Can NanoClaw Itself Talk to Ollama?"
# section for how a group's own model gets set). Empty/unset (the default)
# lets Claude Code pick its own default model. Set via the "Choose Claude
# Model" menu action (scripts/choose-model.sh) rather than by hand — it
# also recreates the container, since a `docker run -e` value only takes
# effect at container creation, not a plain restart.
# Format: A Claude model ID (e.g. claude-sonnet-5) or empty.
#CLAUDE_MODEL=
